oot certificates allow trust in distrusted emSign intermediates","description":"Affected versions include `emSign ECC Root CA - G3`, which can allow certificate\npaths through distrusted emSign intermediates.\n\nAffected versions may accept certificate paths containing distrusted emSign\nintermediate public keys. The private keys corresponding to these intermediates\nare now well known.\n\nVersion 1.0.10+ removes this root.\n\nThe `webpki-roots` 0.26.11 compatibility package contains no independent trust\nstore and re-exports the roots from its separately resolved 1.x dependency.\nThat parent dependency must resolve to 1.0.10 or newer; an older parent remains\naffected by this advisory.","date":"2026-10-19","aliases":["CVE-2026-111943"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["crypto-failure"],"keywords":["certificate","distrust","x509"],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":["https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/","https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2083449"],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/rustls/webpki-roots/pull/133","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=1.0.10"],"unaffected":["=0.26.11"]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"webpki-roots","version":"1.0.9","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"7dcd9d09a39985f5344844e66b0c530a33843579125f23e21e9f0f220850f22a","dependencies":[{"name":"rustls-pki-types","version":"1.15.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}}]},"warnings":{}}
